  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1134 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nThere is a high chance for the high pressure system to remain the \ndominant weather feature across the southern plains for the rest of \nthe week and into next week. Thursday and Friday the position of the \nhigh will most likely be to the west of the southern plans leading \nto a more northwesterly over the southern plains. This will allow \nfor a low chance for rain showers and thunderstorms each day as \nsmall scale weather system can pass across the panhandles. \nTemperatures will most likely remain hot as the high pressure \ncontinues to heat the southern plains. For the weekend and into \nearly next week the high pressure has higher chances than not to \nreposition to be more over the southern plains. This would prevent \nthe passage of weather system keep the panhandles on the drier side. \nStill this would indicate that the heating would be higher during \nthis time. So there can be an uptick in the temperatures for this \nweekend and early next week.",
